{
  "info": {
    "name": "Mailpit Mock API v1.21.3",
    "description": "Test collection for the mock Mailpit service. Base URL defaults to http://localhost:8122. In docker-compose, the service is reachable at http://mailpit-api:8122.\n\nMailpit is MailHog's successor and is deliberately not a reskin of it. Four things drive the API:\n\n**A real search query language.** `query=from:billing is:unread -tag:receipt \"order total\"` -- prefixed terms (`from:`, `to:`, `cc:`, `bcc:`, `reply-to:`, `addressed:`, `subject:`, `message-id:`, `tag:`, `before:`, `after:`), `is:`/`has:` flags, quoted phrases and negation with `-` or `!`, all ANDed.\n\n**A message has state.** Read/unread is tracked and mutable, and `GET /api/v1/message/{id}` marks a message read as a side effect. Tags are first-class: settable, renameable, deletable, searchable.\n\n**Mailpit analyses what it captured.** `html-check` scores the HTML against a client matrix, `link-check` reports what each link answered, `sa-check` returns SpamAssassin rule hits.\n\n**Chaos is error codes, not behaviours.** Each trigger -- Sender, Recipient, Authentication -- carries an SMTP error code and a whole percentage. The roll is seeded from the address, so the same address always meets the same fate.\n\nNote the singular/plural split: `/api/v1/messages` is the list, `/api/v1/message/{id}` is the read. Requests labelled '(N expected)' assert an error path.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8122"
    }
  ],
